ven parabola passes through the point $(-4,-2),$ so we can substitute $x=-4$ and $y=-2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ (-4)^{2} & =4p(-2) \\\\ 16 & =-8p \\\\ p & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(-2)y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-8y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115438/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "281514e9-6e16-5b21-ba4e-503991d811c2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115438"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
